    "notification_text": "+ ADVERTISEMENT FOR THE YOUNG PROFESSIONAL-II (YP-II) Interview (Hybrid mode) for the appointment of a Young Professional-II (YP-II) under the project ‘National Surveillance Programme for Aquatic Animal Diseases - Phase II’ will be held in hybrid mode on 31.08.2026 at 11 AM onwards at ICAR-CIFE, Mumbai. The appointment of the selected candidate will be purely on a contractual basis and shall remain valid until 31 March 2027 or until the termination of the candidate's services for any reason. Post Young Professional-II (YP-II) No of Vacancy| 1 Place of | ICAR-CIFE, Mumbai ~ posting Qualifications] Master of Fisheries Science (M.F.Sc.) in any discipline of Fisheries Science with B.F.Sc./ Candidates with Master’s degree in Zoology/Life Sciences/Marine Biology. Desirable Work experience in Fish Health/ Biotechnology having technical knowledge on PCR based diagnostic techniques. Job Requirement Farm visits, collection of fish and shrimp samples, sample processing and PCR based testing of samples for pathogen screening and disease diagnosis, communication of results ____| with farmers and Report writing. Age Minimum 21 years and Maximum 45 years . Candidates must fill in the application (Annexure I) and email it to gayatrit@cife.edu.in, along with self-attested copies of testimonials and degree certificates. The last date for submission of the application is 26.08.2026. Only shortlisted candidates will be intimated for the interview. The link will be provided in due course to the candidates preferring to attend online. The employment is purely temporary and the incumbent shall not have any claim for regular appointment under ICAR. The decision of the Director, ICAR-CIFE will be final and binding in all respects. The Director, ICAR-CIFE reserve the right to cancel the interview/ appointment without assigning any reason. PRE EOS (Swati S. Koli) Assistant Administrative Officer Annexure I 1. Personal Information: 1. Name po 4. Date of Birth श्््ंा््