    "notification_text": "Advt. No. R&P/305/2024 दिल्‍ली दिश्‍िदिद्यालय UNIVERSITY OF DELHI Page 1 of 1 Scheme of Examination for Screening and or Shortlisting of applicants for Interview applicable for the post code: TDFT01, TDFT02, TDFT03 (Final Selection will be based on Interview/Personal Interaction) A. Scheme of the Examination: Written Test Paper MCQ Type Time: 2 hours* Max. marks: 400 marks (100 questions) Total Marks 400 marks *45 minutes extra would be given to Visually Handicapped, Cerebral Palsy candidates or similarly placed candidates from PwBD category. B. Test components: Subject specific questions as per syllabus of Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering (GATE) as detailed below: Sr. No. Discipline Test Component 1. Computer Engineering (Post Code: TDFT01) As per syllabus prescribed for GATE paper for Computer Science and Information Technology (Copy enclosed) 2. Electrical Engineering (Post Code: TDFT02) As per syllabus prescribed for GATE paper for Electrical Engineering (Copy enclosed) 3. Electronics and Communication Engineering (Post Code: TDFT03) As per syllabus prescribed for GATE paper for Electronics and Communication Engineering (Copy enclosed) Note: 1. All the questions shall be compulsory. Each question carries 04 marks. There shall be negative marking of 01 mark for each wrong answer. The cutoff for qualifying the written test will be 50% marks of the average score of the top 05% of the candidates. There will be a relaxation of 05% marks for candidates belonging to SC, ST and 10% for PwBD category. 2. If the number of candidates qualifying the written test is more, then 30 candidates for the first vacancy and 10 candidates for every additional vacancy, in each category, shall be called for interview in order of their ranks in the merit list prepared on the basis of result of the written test. All candidates having same marks as per the cut off shall be called for the interview. 3. The marks awarded to the candidates in the written test shall not have any weightage/credit or merit during assessment/interview of the candidates by the Selection Committee as these marks shall be used only for screening/shortlisting purposes.",
